the top row shift one position to the right, resulting in the encircled '1'=
s in the bottom row. The remaining bits are filled with '0's.  To the right=
, `dp[x] =3D 2` indicates the initial count of '1's in `x`, and `dp[x >> 1]=
 =3D 2` shows the count of '1's after the right shift.  The diagram visuall=
y demonstrates how the right shift operation moves bits to the right, filli=
ng empty positions with zeros, and how this affects the count of '1's." loa=
